WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.150
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:03.420 --> 00:04.546
PARK MINJAE'S LIST

3
00:04.630 --> 00:05.923
START DATING...

4
00:36.620 --> 00:40.958
BETWEEN STEPS

5
00:41.583 --> 00:43.835
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS, AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

6
00:43.919 --> 00:45.546
THIS DRAMA CONTAINS SENSITIVE CONTENT

7
00:46.672 --> 00:48.882
EPISODE 11

8
00:49.424 --> 00:51.343
[Sejin] I'm so full I'm going to burst.

9
00:52.052 --> 00:53.595
[Taeho] Did you eat a lot?

10
00:55.013 --> 00:56.932
-Oh, right. -Here are your beers.

11
00:57.015 --> 00:58.892
[Taeho] Thank you.

12
00:58.976 --> 01:00.310
[straining] Wait a second.

13
01:01.186 --> 01:02.813
You can give those here.

14
01:02.896 --> 01:04.398
Here's a glass.

15
01:04.481 --> 01:06.108
-All right. -Yeah, here.

16
01:06.191 --> 01:07.484
Could you please take these?

17
01:08.735 --> 01:11.113
-Can I have one? -Let me take the one in there.

18
01:11.196 --> 01:12.823
I'm going to finish Youjin's too.

19
01:13.907 --> 01:14.908
Are we all good?

20
01:16.159 --> 01:18.662
By the way, where did Minjae go?

21
01:18.745 --> 01:20.497
-He wasn't in the bathroom. -He wasn't?

22
01:20.581 --> 01:23.250
It seemed like he was seeing Lim Youjin off.

23
01:23.333 --> 01:27.462
Hmm. Well, then go tell him to hurry back.

24
01:27.546 --> 01:29.631
Beer doesn't taste good when it gets warm.

25
01:32.009 --> 01:33.010
Okay.

26
01:33.885 --> 01:35.304
The beer isn't good.

27
01:35.387 --> 01:36.930
-Oh, boy. -This idiot is drunk.

28
01:37.639 --> 01:39.600
-He left his beer behind. -See you in a bit.

29
01:53.697 --> 01:55.574
Hey. Minjae.

30
02:06.043 --> 02:07.127
-Hey. -Hey.

31
02:09.671 --> 02:11.006
Is Youjin gone?

32
02:12.382 --> 02:13.467
Yeah, she's gone.

33
02:16.928 --> 02:19.723
Taeho says you should hurry back before the beer gets warm.

34
02:21.350 --> 02:22.809
[Minjae] Okay. Let's go.

35
02:42.871 --> 02:45.248
[Youjin] It looks like I'll be a little late. I'm sorry.

36
02:47.793 --> 02:49.419
[Jihoon] Okay. Call me when you get here.

37
02:51.004 --> 02:52.214
Where are you now?

38
02:53.090 --> 02:54.299
Call me when you're here.

39
02:55.967 --> 02:57.427
Are you going to be really late?

40
02:58.679 --> 02:59.680
Where are you?

41
03:00.847 --> 03:02.057
I'm hungry.

42
03:03.517 --> 03:04.810
Hurry up.

43
03:09.022 --> 03:12.025
CALL ME...

44
03:19.741 --> 03:20.909
Let me refill your glass.

45
03:20.992 --> 03:22.035
Okay. Thank you.

46
03:27.833 --> 03:28.834
Excuse me, sir.

47
03:29.584 --> 03:30.752
Just so you know,

48
03:30.836 --> 03:33.588
we stop taking food orders at 8:30.

49
03:33.672 --> 03:34.673
Oh...

50
03:36.591 --> 03:38.718
But it's fine if you're not ordering food.

51
03:39.761 --> 03:41.430
Would you like to see the wine list?

52
03:43.390 --> 03:45.016
No, I'll order food.

53
03:45.100 --> 03:47.269
-Sure. Let me know when you're ready. -Okay.

54
04:02.284 --> 04:03.577
POWER OFF

55
04:09.291 --> 04:14.880
So you're saying you'll have to start your own lab and all that?

56
04:14.963 --> 04:16.089
Yeah, I will.

57
04:18.717 --> 04:20.510
How many students will you take on?

58
04:20.594 --> 04:22.262
Well, I don't have much of a budget,

59
04:22.345 --> 04:24.556
and the lab is pretty small, so I'm not sure.

60
04:25.891 --> 04:27.392
[Taeho] In that case, Minjae,

61
04:27.476 --> 04:29.394
there are a few undergrads I've had my eye on.

62
04:29.478 --> 04:31.396
I'll tell them to reach out to you.

63
04:32.814 --> 04:35.108
We can take care of it ourselves.

64
04:35.192 --> 04:36.985
You're leaving for your postdoc anyway.

65
04:37.068 --> 04:38.653
We'll take care of it.

66
04:38.737 --> 04:41.406
If you have to go, you have to go. Just go.

67
04:41.490 --> 04:42.949
-Wow. -He says just go.

68
04:43.658 --> 04:45.494
[scoffs] You little...

69
04:46.745 --> 04:48.413
Huh? Jeez.

70
04:49.122 --> 04:53.376
You guys are treating me like some washed-up old man already.

71
04:53.460 --> 04:54.503
How dare you...

72
04:54.586 --> 04:56.755
Hey, forget it. Don't worry about it.

73
04:56.838 --> 04:58.799
You guys just focus on your own lab.

74
04:58.882 --> 05:00.008
I can take care of mine.

75
05:00.091 --> 05:02.219
Come on, Minjae. Jeez.

76
05:02.302 --> 05:04.012
I won't be away for long. Okay?

77
05:04.095 --> 05:06.223
I'll be back in Korea in just a year, you know?

78
05:07.474 --> 05:09.518
Whatever. You go wherever you have to go.

79
05:09.601 --> 05:11.144
We'll talk once you're back.

80
05:11.978 --> 05:13.313
Hey, order some more beer.

81
05:13.396 --> 05:15.357
What, more beer? You've had enough.

82
05:16.358 --> 05:17.734
I didn't even drink that much.

83
05:18.485 --> 05:20.695
Hey, just drink mine... Actually, just order it.

84
05:21.321 --> 05:23.073
Could we get some more beer, please?

85
05:23.156 --> 05:24.950
-How many? -Wait, hold on.

86
05:25.033 --> 05:28.328
Then, Minjae, should we go somewhere else for another round?

87
05:28.411 --> 05:30.747
How about the whelk place?

88
05:30.831 --> 05:32.249
That sounds great.

89
05:32.332 --> 05:33.792
We've just had something fried,

90
05:33.875 --> 05:35.669
-so soju would be refreshing. -Yeah.

91
05:35.752 --> 05:38.505
Whelk? Is there a whelk place nearby...

92
05:38.630 --> 05:41.049
No, don't bother looking. I know a place.

93
05:41.132 --> 05:42.467
It's right around the corner.

94
05:42.551 --> 05:46.179
But Chansoo has to take the subway all the way to Incheon.

95
05:46.263 --> 05:48.932
He'd be pretty tired if he went for another round.

96
05:49.015 --> 05:50.350
-[Minjae] Yeah. -What?

97
05:51.560 --> 05:53.895
And Lee Kangin has a Champions League match tonight.

98
05:53.979 --> 05:55.272
-You can't miss that. -Oh!

99
05:55.981 --> 05:57.566
What time is the Champions League?

100
05:57.649 --> 05:58.859
Around 3 or so.

101
05:58.942 --> 06:00.902
Yeah. Just go home and watch that.

102
06:00.986 --> 06:02.654
Let's go now. Come on, get up.

103
06:02.737 --> 06:06.575
[groans] There's no need to travel all the way back to Incheon, right?

104
06:07.409 --> 06:09.244
We can just watch it at Sejin's.

105
06:09.327 --> 06:10.662
-[Hangyeol] Right. -What?

106
06:10.745 --> 06:14.457
I mean, we can just get the whelks and some other food to go, right?

107
06:14.541 --> 06:16.710
Then have another round at your place. Okay?

108
06:16.793 --> 06:18.670
And we can all watch the game together,

109
06:18.753 --> 06:22.799
and then all head to work together tomorrow afternoon.

110
06:22.883 --> 06:24.092
-[Chansoo] Sounds great. -[Taeho] Yeah.

111
06:24.175 --> 06:25.594
-[Chansoo] I'd love that. -[Hangyeol] Sounds perfect.

112
06:25.677 --> 06:28.263
[Minjae] Drink and watch the game all night, then go to work?

113
06:28.346 --> 06:29.347
Yeah. Why?

114
06:29.431 --> 06:30.891
Aren't you going to be tired?

115
06:30.974 --> 06:32.392
[Taeho] Why would I be tired?

116
06:32.475 --> 06:35.186
And I'm the leader of this lab. If I say we do it, we do it.

117
06:35.270 --> 06:36.563
You don't get a say, okay?

118
06:36.646 --> 06:38.064
Have it your way.

119
06:38.148 --> 06:39.316
[Taeho grunts] Hmm.

120
06:39.858 --> 06:44.112
So we'll get the whelks to go and pick up drinks at a convenience store.

121
06:44.195 --> 06:45.864
-[Taeho] Yeah, soju's cheaper there. -[Chansoo] Right.

122
06:45.947 --> 06:50.910
No. The thing is, my home isn't particularly ready for guests right now.

123
06:52.787 --> 06:53.788
Why not?

124
06:53.872 --> 06:55.290
My place...

125
06:56.249 --> 06:57.876
It's really drafty.

126
06:57.959 --> 06:59.294
Cold air just comes right in.

127
06:59.377 --> 07:01.087
I'm fine because I'm used to it,

128
07:01.171 --> 07:05.216
but you guys will freeze and end up getting sick or something.

129
07:05.300 --> 07:06.801
You've got heat, damn it.

130
07:06.885 --> 07:09.971
Just crank it up! Get the place nice and warm. Don't be cheap.

131
07:10.055 --> 07:11.097
I'm not being cheap.

132
07:11.181 --> 07:12.432
Jeez.

133
07:13.600 --> 07:17.937
I'm saying, because of the windows, no matter how I...

134
07:18.021 --> 07:19.939
Anyway, it just won't work.

135
07:20.023 --> 07:22.484
It's just too cold. You'll freeze to death.

136
07:22.567 --> 07:25.070
If it's cold, we can just get under some blankets.

137
07:25.153 --> 07:27.447
Watching the game together will be so much fun.

138
07:27.530 --> 07:30.450
Yeah. All right, so this...

139
07:30.533 --> 07:33.203
this is our last drink here.

140
07:33.286 --> 07:35.205
-Let's finish this and get going. -Okay.

141
07:36.373 --> 07:38.166
Then how about...

142
07:38.833 --> 07:39.834
[Taeho] Yeah.

143
07:40.335 --> 07:41.670
Minjae's place?

144
07:41.753 --> 07:42.962
[Minjae] What?

145
07:43.046 --> 07:44.089
My place?

146
07:44.172 --> 07:46.633
Your new apartment. It's in Seocho-dong, right?

147
07:46.716 --> 07:47.717
What?

148
07:48.385 --> 07:50.929
Dream Sun Palace in Seocho-dong.

149
07:52.514 --> 07:54.391
-And it's on the 33rd floor. -Thirty...

150
07:54.474 --> 07:56.643
The view from up there must be amazing at night.

151
07:58.645 --> 08:01.439
We can't go to Seocho-dong at this hour. It's too far.

152
08:01.523 --> 08:04.401
No, Minjae. It'll only take 15, 20 minutes by taxi at this hour.

153
08:04.484 --> 08:06.486
[Minjae] The taxi is going to cost too much. Forget it.

154
08:06.569 --> 08:08.488
He's got at least two bathrooms

155
08:08.571 --> 08:13.284
and a living room, where there's almost definitely a TV.

156
08:13.368 --> 08:15.161
-[Taeho] Of course. -[Chansoo] Well, it's an apartment.

157
08:15.245 --> 08:16.913
-Of course it's got it. -Yeah.

158
08:16.996 --> 08:19.457
[Hangyeol] This can be a welcome-back and housewarming party.

159
08:19.541 --> 08:22.836
Yeah. Kill two birds with one stone, as they say.

160
08:22.919 --> 08:25.672
Yeah. Looks like we've picked the perfect day.

161
08:25.755 --> 08:29.426
All right, then... Everyone, drink up what's left in your glass and get up.

162
08:29.509 --> 08:31.177
-Okay. -All right. Cheers.

163
08:31.261 --> 08:33.096
-Cheers. -Cheers. I've finished mine.

164
08:33.179 --> 08:34.848
-Drink this. -You're not going to?

165
08:34.931 --> 08:36.433
-No, you drink it. -Give it to me.

166
08:38.226 --> 08:40.687
I've never told you where I live. How did you know?

167
08:40.770 --> 08:42.147
It was written...

168
08:43.231 --> 08:46.026
on the package we got at the lab. I saw it there.

169
08:46.109 --> 08:47.360
You're unbelievable.

170
08:47.444 --> 08:50.989
I looked it up, and apparently, Seocho-dong isn't that far from campus.

171
08:51.072 --> 08:52.282
Can I come over often?

172
08:55.118 --> 08:57.495
Excuse me. Could we have the leftover chicken to go?

173
08:58.705 --> 08:59.706
[Taeho] All right.

174
09:04.919 --> 09:06.546
Sir, may I clear the plate for you?

175
09:07.297 --> 09:08.882
-Yes. -All right.

176
09:11.926 --> 09:14.471
For dessert, we have coffee. Would you like some?

177
09:17.265 --> 09:18.391
No, I'm good.

178
09:19.184 --> 09:20.185
All right.

179
09:50.381 --> 09:53.760
[staff] That will be 51,000 won. Please insert your card.

180
09:53.843 --> 09:55.428
Would you like a receipt?

181
09:55.512 --> 09:56.513
[Jihoon] No, thanks.

182
09:56.596 --> 09:58.223
[staff] You're all set. Thank you.

183
10:33.258 --> 10:34.467
What are you doing here?

184
10:38.555 --> 10:40.598
-Sorry, I'm late. -I said, what are you doing here?

185
10:41.933 --> 10:44.435
I spotted this car on my way over.

186
10:45.687 --> 10:49.232
I took a closer look, and it looked like your car.

187
10:49.315 --> 10:50.942
So I was wondering if it was yours...

188
10:52.068 --> 10:53.903
and I guess it really was yours.

189
10:55.613 --> 10:56.739
This is a parking lot.

190
10:57.824 --> 10:59.993
The restaurant over there is where you eat.

191
11:01.035 --> 11:03.163
-I'm sorry. -You already said you're sorry.

192
11:05.331 --> 11:07.333
Well, I was going to call you. But...

193
11:15.049 --> 11:16.217
You're freezing.

194
11:22.765 --> 11:24.601
Have you eaten?

195
11:28.897 --> 11:30.440
Why haven't you eaten yet?

196
11:34.569 --> 11:36.946
It's okay. Skipping a meal won't kill you.

197
11:41.784 --> 11:43.494
I'm sorry I'm late.

198
11:43.578 --> 11:45.163
I told you, you already said that.

199
11:50.752 --> 11:52.045
You're here now.

200
11:56.591 --> 11:57.800
That's all that matters.

201
11:59.594 --> 12:01.971
How long are we going to be standing here like this?

202
12:02.055 --> 12:03.056
[Jihoon] All night.

203
12:05.225 --> 12:06.768
We'll stay like this all night.

204
12:10.647 --> 12:11.648
Why?

205
12:13.650 --> 12:15.401
You've got other plans?

206
12:20.573 --> 12:21.658
Have you been crying?

207
12:22.700 --> 12:24.118
No, I haven't.

208
12:27.580 --> 12:29.415
-[automated voice] Going down. -Isn't it here?

209
12:29.499 --> 12:30.625
Aren't we getting off?

210
12:30.708 --> 12:31.709
Right. It's here.

211
12:33.044 --> 12:34.045
Come this way.

212
12:35.505 --> 12:37.048
It's so nice here.

213
12:46.099 --> 12:47.100
Jeez.

214
12:49.978 --> 12:52.480
Coming in. [chuckling]

215
12:53.815 --> 12:54.816
Coming through.

216
12:54.899 --> 12:56.734
-Your home. -Excuse me.

217
13:01.072 --> 13:02.073
All right.

218
13:02.156 --> 13:04.284
Minjae, how do you turn on the light?

219
13:07.370 --> 13:08.705
-[Chansoo] Where is it? -[Minjae grunts]

220
13:23.678 --> 13:25.680
I don't think we can see the Hangang River.

221
13:25.763 --> 13:27.849
-[Taeho] Right? But the view is nice. -[Hangyeol] The view is nice.

222
13:28.599 --> 13:30.351
We're in Gangnam, so that makes sense.

223
13:30.435 --> 13:32.312
-We're facing away from it. -That's right.

224
13:32.395 --> 13:33.896
This is...

225
13:33.980 --> 13:35.315
[Minjae] Guys, wash your hands first.

226
13:35.398 --> 13:37.275
[Sejin] Excuse me. I'll use the bathroom.

227
13:42.071 --> 13:44.073
[Taeho] This is a walk-in closet.

228
13:44.157 --> 13:45.241
[Chansoo] I can't see anything.

229
13:45.324 --> 13:47.035
-There's nothing. -Minjae, one second.

230
13:52.290 --> 13:53.708
[Chansoo] Hangyeol.

231
13:53.791 --> 13:55.460
Hangyeol, what are you trying on?

232
13:58.337 --> 13:59.881
[Taeho] It looks pretty good on you.

233
13:59.964 --> 14:01.799
-[Hangyeol] Minjae. -Yeah?

234
14:01.883 --> 14:03.843
I've never seen you wear this hat.

235
14:04.510 --> 14:06.345
If you don't wear it, can I have it?

236
14:07.638 --> 14:10.058
I wear it. Put it back. Come on, put it back.

237
14:10.141 --> 14:12.101
-But I've never seen you wear it. -I do.

238
14:13.311 --> 14:15.438
-Minjae, how about this one? -[Minjae] What?

239
14:15.521 --> 14:16.773
Do you wear this too?

240
14:16.856 --> 14:17.857
I do... [groans softly]

241
14:18.399 --> 14:20.276
I do. Come on, put it back...

242
14:20.359 --> 14:22.487
What are you doing? Just come sit down already!

243
14:22.570 --> 14:24.655
-[Taeho] What'd you think of this one? -[Chansoo] It's nice.

244
14:24.739 --> 14:27.075
-[Hangyeol] What's that? -[Taeho] Obviously, it's Minjae's.

245
14:27.158 --> 14:28.367
-[laughing] -[Chansoo] It's Minjae's?

246
14:28.451 --> 14:29.535
-[Taeho] Yeah. -[Hangyeol] This one?

247
14:29.619 --> 14:31.037
Hey, he's going to get mad at you.

248
14:31.120 --> 14:32.205
[Taeho] It's okay.

249
14:32.288 --> 14:33.915
God damn it.

250
14:34.582 --> 14:35.833
[Taeho] Hey, Hangyeol, you...

251
14:35.917 --> 14:38.127
Those pants are pretty nice. Yeah.

252
14:38.211 --> 14:40.046
-[Chansoo] You're wearing his pants? -Damn it.

253
14:40.713 --> 14:42.715
[Taeho] Well, he's also...

254
14:42.799 --> 14:44.759
He's pretty tall, so he pulls it off nicely.

255
14:44.842 --> 14:47.386
-[continues indistinctly] -[sighs] God damn it. For God's sake.

256
15:09.242 --> 15:11.327
[Taeho laughing] You can't pull it off.

257
15:11.410 --> 15:13.204
-[Chansoo] Come on, why? -[laughter continues]

258
15:22.797 --> 15:24.048
Damn it.

259
17:09.403 --> 17:10.655
[Jihoon] Try it.

260
17:11.155 --> 17:12.990
You said you liked it the other day.

261
17:17.286 --> 17:19.914
Do you want something else? Should I order something else?

262
17:22.750 --> 17:24.877
Do you want to go home? Should I take you home?

263
17:30.007 --> 17:31.342
You don't want to go home.

264
17:31.425 --> 17:33.511
Do you want to go somewhere else instead?

265
17:36.556 --> 17:37.557
Hmm?

266
17:42.103 --> 17:43.896
Tell me. What do you want to eat?

267
17:45.648 --> 17:47.817
I just don't want to eat anything.

268
17:47.900 --> 17:49.235
I can't get anything down.

269
17:52.655 --> 17:54.407
-Professor. -Yes.

270
17:54.490 --> 17:58.411
We had some abalone left over today, so I made some abalone porridge.

271
18:00.371 --> 18:02.540
Abalone porridge would be great. Thank you, sir.

272
18:02.623 --> 18:05.418
-Sure. -No, I'm okay. I can just eat this.

273
18:08.087 --> 18:10.047
-We'll have the porridge, please. -[staff] Okay.

274
18:12.008 --> 18:13.050
-Thank you. -Sure.

275
18:14.302 --> 18:16.137
But I don't want abalone porridge.

276
18:16.887 --> 18:18.889
Why come if you'll just say no to everything?

277
18:18.973 --> 18:20.266
Just to give me a hard time?

278
18:22.310 --> 18:24.478
Well, because you asked me to come out...

279
18:30.568 --> 18:33.821
You said you got me a gift. Give it to me.

280
18:33.904 --> 18:35.239
I didn't. There's nothing.

281
18:54.467 --> 18:57.011
I'll give it to you if you eat the abalone porridge.

282
19:08.230 --> 19:09.273
Can I open it?

283
19:33.631 --> 19:34.799
Do you want to try it on?

284
19:35.591 --> 19:36.592
Well...

285
19:41.514 --> 19:44.141
What's wrong? You don't like it?

286
19:44.225 --> 19:45.893
No, that's not it.

287
19:46.519 --> 19:48.938
-It seems too expensive, so... -It's not that expensive.

288
19:51.148 --> 19:54.193
It's too much. I don't think I can accept it. I'm sorry.

289
19:59.532 --> 20:00.950
But I bought it for you.

290
20:05.079 --> 20:06.455
I bought it for you.

291
20:06.539 --> 20:07.581
I don't want it.

292
20:11.502 --> 20:13.754
People who don't know might get the wrong idea,

293
20:14.588 --> 20:18.259
and I don't want any weird rumors to start about you because of me.

294
20:18.342 --> 20:19.343
I don't want that.

295
20:20.761 --> 20:21.762
What rumors?

296
20:23.514 --> 20:25.474
About us seeing each other or something.

297
20:25.558 --> 20:27.476
Apparently, some students are saying that.

298
20:28.769 --> 20:31.981
You know how some people at school spread weird rumors like that.

299
20:35.484 --> 20:36.485
I don't care.

300
20:37.987 --> 20:38.988
Pardon?

301
20:39.864 --> 20:41.991
The rumors and the people talking about it.

302
20:43.033 --> 20:45.411
I'm not afraid of any of that, and I don't care.

303
20:46.537 --> 20:47.538
Well, but--

304
20:47.621 --> 20:49.665
Giving pretty things to the woman I like

305
20:51.041 --> 20:53.210
and making her happy.

306
20:54.920 --> 20:56.088
That's enough for me.

307
21:03.262 --> 21:06.223
But I already like someone.

308
21:09.935 --> 21:12.062
I already like someone.

309
21:18.444 --> 21:19.528
Okay.

310
21:23.741 --> 21:25.326
So keep liking him.

311
21:26.160 --> 21:27.161
What?

312
21:27.703 --> 21:30.080
You can keep liking him. It's okay.

313
21:34.585 --> 21:35.753
But I...

314
21:37.505 --> 21:40.090
can't reciprocate your feelings.

315
21:41.175 --> 21:44.094
What matters is that I gave you my whole heart.

316
21:44.178 --> 21:46.263
Who cares if it's not reciprocated?

317
21:46.347 --> 21:48.098
We don't have to keep score like this.

318
21:52.478 --> 21:53.896
So, Youjin, you should...

319
21:56.357 --> 21:58.359
Why do you make yourself suffer so much?

320
21:59.944 --> 22:02.696
You think his feelings for you aren't as deep as yours,

321
22:02.780 --> 22:06.075
and you resent him for it, like you've somehow lost out.

322
22:06.158 --> 22:07.368
You don't have to do that.

323
22:08.118 --> 22:11.205
-That's not what it is. -That's exactly what it is. I'm right.

324
22:14.583 --> 22:17.086
Who said I wanted him to feel exactly the same way I do,

325
22:17.878 --> 22:19.922
as if our feelings were balanced on scales?

326
22:20.005 --> 22:21.215
That's not what I mean.

327
22:22.883 --> 22:25.719
I gave him my whole heart, my everything.

328
22:27.471 --> 22:29.723
But he betrayed it all and just threw it away.

329
22:30.975 --> 22:31.976
He's a traitor.

330
22:34.979 --> 22:37.940
And it put me through so much pain, I felt like I could die.

331
22:43.237 --> 22:44.905
That's what love does.

332
22:46.824 --> 22:49.118
It leaves you a complete train wreck.

333
22:51.245 --> 22:54.957
A train wreck is someone who's completely wrecked, like a derailed train.

334
22:55.040 --> 22:57.293
That's what loving someone can do to you.

335
22:58.794 --> 23:03.591
You give them the power to wreck your heart at any moment.

336
23:06.218 --> 23:08.012
I don't want to give anyone that power.

337
23:08.095 --> 23:09.221
Even if you don't,

338
23:10.723 --> 23:13.475
you can't just take the good stuff and skip the bad.

339
23:13.559 --> 23:16.520
They're two sides of the same coin. It's just the way it is.

340
23:22.735 --> 23:25.946
Otherwise, it's not love. It's all fake and a lie.

341
23:30.993 --> 23:32.786
So stop being stubborn

342
23:33.996 --> 23:35.539
and just keep liking him

343
23:36.540 --> 23:38.250
as much as you want,

344
23:38.334 --> 23:39.752
as much as you can.

345
23:44.214 --> 23:45.424
Keep liking him.

346
23:47.217 --> 23:49.303
Until those feelings wear themselves out.

347
25:35.659 --> 25:39.038
MOVE TO TRASH

348
25:40.789 --> 25:41.832
CANCEL

349
26:56.782 --> 27:01.370
MOVE TO TRASH

350
27:05.916 --> 27:07.793
MOVE TO TRASH

351
29:10.165 --> 29:12.459
Looks like he doesn't have any big plates.

352
29:12.542 --> 29:16.004
Forget it. Just bring the whole pan here.

353
29:17.172 --> 29:18.173
Okay.

354
29:33.981 --> 29:35.983
Jeez.

355
29:39.611 --> 29:40.946
Hey, Kim Sejin.

356
29:41.613 --> 29:43.699
Go tell the guys to come and eat.

357
29:46.118 --> 29:47.119
Okay.

358
29:49.413 --> 29:52.082
Chansoo. Hangyeol.

359
29:53.583 --> 29:55.168
He says come eat the pajeon first.

360
29:55.252 --> 29:56.837
-Right. Okay. -We'll be right out.

361
29:56.962 --> 29:59.006
-After this round. -We'll be right there.

362
29:59.673 --> 30:00.924
-[Chansoo] Damn it. -[Hangyeol]There you go.

363
30:01.717 --> 30:02.968
[Chansoo] What's wrong with this?

364
30:03.051 --> 30:04.219
[Sejin] Hurry up.

365
30:05.345 --> 30:07.055
They say they'll be right here.

366
30:07.139 --> 30:09.558
Okay. Go get Minjae too.

367
30:10.183 --> 30:11.977
Tell him to come out and eat with us.

368
30:12.060 --> 30:13.979
I think he's asleep.

369
30:14.062 --> 30:15.731
Then wake him up. [clicks tongue]

370
30:15.814 --> 30:18.400
Tell him the game starts soon, so he should come quickly.

371
30:19.901 --> 30:21.737
[clicks tongue] Come on!

372
30:26.324 --> 30:27.325
Jeez.

373
30:30.120 --> 30:32.622
Minjae, are you asleep?

374
30:34.207 --> 30:35.834
Come out and have some pajeon.

375
30:45.844 --> 30:48.138
Hey, Chansoo, Hangyeol, come on out!

376
30:48.221 --> 30:50.640
Minjae, are you okay?

377
30:50.724 --> 30:54.436
Yeah, I'm okay.

378
30:59.399 --> 31:01.318
Wait, careful. Wait.

379
31:04.571 --> 31:07.532
Careful. Be careful. Oh, boy.

380
31:11.369 --> 31:13.121
-It's okay. -[gags]

381
31:20.212 --> 31:23.090
[Sejin] Minjae, are you okay?

382
31:23.173 --> 31:25.675
Do you want me to get you some stomach medicine?

383
31:25.759 --> 31:27.219
[Minjae] No, I'm fine.

384
31:27.302 --> 31:28.595
Go. I'm fine.

385
31:39.189 --> 31:40.190
Oh, man.

386
31:46.029 --> 31:48.240
What's up? He doesn't want to come out?

387
31:48.323 --> 31:49.449
No.

388
31:49.991 --> 31:51.910
It looks like he's feeling sick.

389
31:51.993 --> 31:53.745
I don't think he's going to eat this.

390
31:54.371 --> 31:56.123
Why? Why is he feeling sick?

391
31:58.542 --> 31:59.876
Could it be indigestion?

392
32:00.669 --> 32:02.587
He barely drank anything, though.

393
32:03.630 --> 32:05.757
Not sure. I think he has a bit of a fever, too.

394
32:05.841 --> 32:07.425
Maybe it's a cold.

395
32:07.509 --> 32:10.262
Well, he was busy with the move and everything.

396
32:10.345 --> 32:11.596
That must be why he's sick.

397
32:12.472 --> 32:15.267
I wonder if any pharmacies are still open this late.

398
32:15.350 --> 32:17.686
Hey, if the pharmacies are closed,

399
32:17.769 --> 32:20.021
you can get cold medicine at convenience stores...

400
32:22.524 --> 32:24.776
Hey, Sejin. Wait, you...

401
32:26.194 --> 32:27.279
Hey, this...

402
32:27.362 --> 32:28.446
What's this?

403
32:29.197 --> 32:31.408
It must be from when Minjae threw up earlier.

404
32:31.491 --> 32:32.492
[Taeho] What the...

405
32:34.911 --> 32:37.455
Hey, call 119. Now!

406
32:38.456 --> 32:39.833
[Chansoo] Wait, why? What's wrong?

407
32:39.916 --> 32:41.209
-What's up? -[Taeho] Hey, Minjae.

408
32:41.293 --> 32:42.294
[Chansoo] I don't know.

409
32:42.377 --> 32:46.214
Hey. Open your eyes. Hey. Minjae!

410
32:46.298 --> 32:47.382
[Hangyeol]Minjae, what's up?

411
32:48.383 --> 32:49.384
My phone!

412
33:20.999 --> 33:27.088
RESTRICTED AREA

413
33:31.259 --> 33:34.387
A patient named Park Minjae was brought in a little while ago.

414
33:34.471 --> 33:35.680
Where is he?

415
33:35.764 --> 33:37.724
-He was throwing up blood. -[telephone ringing]

416
33:37.807 --> 33:38.808
Excuse me.

417
33:39.643 --> 33:41.686
Hello, this is Nurse Jo Geonu in the ER.

418
33:42.979 --> 33:43.980
Yes.

419
33:45.106 --> 33:46.983
The MRI scan's just finished?

420
33:48.401 --> 33:50.195
-I'm kind of tied up here. -Yeah, Taeho.

421
33:50.278 --> 33:52.656
We just got to the ER. Where are you?

422
33:54.991 --> 33:56.326
-Taeho. -Hey.

423
33:57.160 --> 33:59.371
I said you didn't need to come. Why did you come?

424
33:59.454 --> 34:00.538
Where's Minjae?

425
34:00.622 --> 34:02.749
He just went in for a test.

426
34:03.875 --> 34:06.670
But why did he throw up blood all of a sudden?

427
34:07.295 --> 34:09.714
I don't know. I guess the test will tell.

428
34:09.798 --> 34:12.425
It's not life-threatening or anything, right?

429
34:12.509 --> 34:14.219
Dude, don't freaking jinx it.

430
34:14.970 --> 34:17.472
He's fine. It's not a big deal.

431
34:17.555 --> 34:19.266
It's probably not a big deal.

432
34:19.349 --> 34:20.392
Yeah.

433
34:21.518 --> 34:23.853
It's not a big deal, and we're just overreacting.

434
34:23.937 --> 34:24.938
Taeho is right.

435
34:25.897 --> 34:27.941
Not really. Minjae has cancer.

436
34:30.235 --> 34:33.405
I heard he had surgery

437
34:34.239 --> 34:35.824
and went through chemo in Canada.

438
34:36.283 --> 34:37.284
Huh?

439
34:39.744 --> 34:41.746
Shouldn't we call his house, too?

440
34:43.248 --> 34:45.750
But there's no one there.

441
34:58.930 --> 35:00.515
Jeez, this place...

442
35:09.024 --> 35:10.025
What?

443
35:10.650 --> 35:11.693
Oh, my goodness.

444
35:11.776 --> 35:13.612
Why is it so messy here?

445
35:15.363 --> 35:16.573
Park Minjae!

446
35:17.616 --> 35:20.327
Come on out. Minjae.

447
35:22.329 --> 35:23.330
Huh?

448
35:33.465 --> 35:34.716
My goodness.

449
35:55.111 --> 35:57.155
Jeez. Seriously.

450
35:59.574 --> 36:03.119
Where on earth did he go even without his phone?

451
36:04.746 --> 36:07.207
And he left the whole place a complete mess.

452
36:08.375 --> 36:10.960
You're in big trouble when you get home, young man.

453
36:11.044 --> 36:12.671
Unbelievable.

454
36:13.963 --> 36:16.299
And what's all this on the table...

455
36:20.720 --> 36:21.763
What's this?

456
36:38.988 --> 36:40.615
-[footsteps approaching] -[door slams]

457
36:43.410 --> 36:44.786
Yes, hello? [panting]

458
36:44.869 --> 36:46.538
[Jaehong] Hi. Who's this?

459
36:46.621 --> 36:48.790
It's not Sejin this time. It's you, Youjin.

460
36:49.499 --> 36:51.209
Where did Sejin go?

461
36:51.292 --> 36:52.585
Kim Sejin?

462
36:53.545 --> 36:57.048
Uh, Sejin went to the restroom.

463
36:57.799 --> 36:59.801
Yeah, that's why I picked up.

464
36:59.884 --> 37:03.471
I see. Then... Chansoo came in today, right?

465
37:03.555 --> 37:07.308
Chansoo? Yes. He did. He came in.

466
37:07.392 --> 37:09.894
[Jaehong] Well, you know that experiment from last week?

467
37:09.978 --> 37:12.063
I wanted to ask him to bring the data up here.

468
37:13.148 --> 37:14.315
Yes, right now.

469
37:18.069 --> 37:19.070
He's not there?

470
37:19.154 --> 37:23.032
No. I mean, he came in, and he was here until just a little while ago,

471
37:24.367 --> 37:28.079
but a meeting with an outside visitor suddenly came up.

472
37:28.163 --> 37:29.998
Yeah. So he stepped out for a bit.

473
37:30.081 --> 37:32.292
An outside visitor? An outside visitor who?

474
37:32.375 --> 37:34.294
No, nothing like that was on the schedule.

475
37:34.377 --> 37:37.172
Uh... I'm not sure who it is.

476
37:38.590 --> 37:41.092
Well, it came up all of a sudden, so he had to rush out,

477
37:41.176 --> 37:43.136
which is why he didn't tell you beforehand.

478
37:43.219 --> 37:44.220
[Jaehong] He rushed out?

479
37:44.304 --> 37:46.181
Where? Why would he rush out?

480
37:47.348 --> 37:49.184
Did you guys get in trouble again?

481
37:49.934 --> 37:52.771
Put Taeho... Put Taeho on the phone. Come on, hurry.

482
37:53.688 --> 37:55.732
Taeho is not at his desk right now.

483
37:56.608 --> 37:59.652
He just went to a nearby...

484
38:00.653 --> 38:03.490
[sighs] ...restroom. Yeah.

485
38:05.158 --> 38:08.536
He went to a nearby restroom?

486
38:10.997 --> 38:11.998
All right.

487
38:25.804 --> 38:28.264
Look at the time. And four of you still aren't here?

488
38:30.099 --> 38:31.935
I guess I've been too easy on you.

489
38:32.018 --> 38:35.355
You know there's nothing I hate more than people being late, right?

490
38:36.356 --> 38:37.357
Yes.

491
38:38.483 --> 38:43.738
Have I ever nagged you even once

492
38:44.781 --> 38:49.244
about your research performance or how your experiments are going?

493
38:50.954 --> 38:52.497
No, right?

494
38:52.580 --> 38:55.792
All I ask is that you show up on time, answer the phone politely...

495
38:55.875 --> 38:57.836
[yelling] ...and don't lie to me!

496
38:59.462 --> 39:03.633
Haven't I told you many times that's all I ask?

497
39:05.426 --> 39:06.469
Yes, you have.

498
39:08.388 --> 39:11.432
These lazy, idle bastards...

499
39:12.600 --> 39:13.852
are all dead today.

500
39:15.645 --> 39:18.106
This is my fault. It's on me.

501
39:21.359 --> 39:23.444
-Put that down. Put it down. -What?

502
39:23.528 --> 39:24.529
Don't.

503
39:25.697 --> 39:26.990
For every minute they're late,

504
39:27.073 --> 39:29.409
-they're getting one whack with the bat. -[phone vibrating]

505
39:32.287 --> 39:34.455
And Taeho, who's supposed to be the lab lead,

506
39:34.539 --> 39:35.707
deserves it the most.

507
39:36.666 --> 39:39.377
So instead of getting your ass over here right now,

508
39:39.460 --> 39:41.796
you have the nerve to call your professor, you punk?

509
39:41.880 --> 39:44.632
You! Have you lost your damn mind?

510
39:45.967 --> 39:47.969
What do you mean, listen?

511
39:49.637 --> 39:51.055
Which hospital?

512
39:54.058 --> 39:55.935
Seohan National University Hospital? Why?

513
39:59.272 --> 40:00.273
Yeah.

514
40:03.109 --> 40:04.110
Yeah, and?

515
40:06.446 --> 40:09.324
Yeah. Minjae threw up blood?

516
40:11.868 --> 40:15.663
I mean, throwing up blood means... he actually vomited blood, right?

517
40:17.999 --> 40:20.543
Okay, he needs surgery. Okay.

518
40:22.086 --> 40:25.256
A procedure? What's the difference between surgery and a procedure?

519
40:25.840 --> 40:26.841
Yeah.

520
40:29.093 --> 40:33.431
[sighs] It's lucky you guys happened to be there with him.

521
40:34.807 --> 40:38.186
Yeah. Imagine if he'd been home alone. That could've been really bad.

522
40:39.020 --> 40:40.313
Talk about a stroke of luck.

523
40:40.396 --> 40:42.023
Why? Who had surgery?

524
40:43.399 --> 40:46.694
Well, Youjin is here, so don't worry about us here.

525
40:46.778 --> 40:49.697
Yeah, I guess you guys should stay there then.

526
40:49.781 --> 40:52.450
Yeah. I'm sure it's hectic over there, so...

527
40:52.533 --> 40:54.035
All right. Bye.

528
40:56.204 --> 40:58.247
What happened? Who had surgery?

529
40:58.331 --> 41:00.291
[sighs] Apparently,

530
41:01.250 --> 41:03.002
Minjae threw up blood last night.

531
41:05.421 --> 41:08.174
Well, he's not in a really serious condition or anything.

532
41:09.175 --> 41:11.511
They say he needs some kind of surgery or procedure.

533
41:13.846 --> 41:15.890
Yeah. Well, it's nothing major, though.

534
41:15.974 --> 41:18.685
They say it's a simple procedure to stop the bleeding,

535
41:18.768 --> 41:20.144
so we shouldn't worry.

536
41:20.895 --> 41:22.146
-Okay. -Yeah.

537
41:22.897 --> 41:26.651
Anyway, looks like you'll have to work by yourself today.

538
41:27.694 --> 41:28.778
-Okay. -Yeah.

539
41:29.654 --> 41:32.865
From now on, just tell me the truth.

540
41:33.992 --> 41:34.993
See you later.

541
41:49.549 --> 41:53.428
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

542
42:07.608 --> 42:10.445
Hi, I'm the guardian of patient Park Minjae.

543
42:10.528 --> 42:12.155
One moment, please.

544
42:13.781 --> 42:15.783
What's your relationship to the patient?

545
42:16.784 --> 42:18.828
I'm his mother.

546
42:42.477 --> 42:44.187
-[knocking at door] -[door sliding]

547
42:45.855 --> 42:47.190
What...

548
42:49.901 --> 42:51.110
Oh, my gosh.

549
42:51.194 --> 42:53.279
You can't sleep in this bed.

550
42:55.740 --> 42:56.741
Sorry.

551
42:57.992 --> 43:00.119
Who is Mr. Park Minjae's guardian?

552
43:00.203 --> 43:01.204
Right, it's me.

553
43:01.287 --> 43:04.207
No, I'm Park Minjae's guardian. [grunts]

554
43:09.545 --> 43:13.007
So it was his mother back then.

555
43:15.968 --> 43:17.887
That was definitely my mistake.

556
43:22.809 --> 43:24.268
GASTROENTEROLOGIST JEONG YEONGJU

557
43:24.352 --> 43:27.647
We performed an emergency endoscopy and ligated the bleeding vessel.

558
43:27.730 --> 43:30.858
Uh, the bleeding has been successfully controlled.

559
43:30.942 --> 43:34.779
We'd like to keep him in the hospital and monitor him for any further bleeding.

560
43:35.905 --> 43:38.282
What about his fever and inflammatory markers?

561
43:38.366 --> 43:43.121
The fever and sore throat he has are just symptoms of a mild cold.

562
43:43.204 --> 43:45.081
It's nothing to be too concerned about.

563
43:45.164 --> 43:47.708
So he's okay?

564
43:47.792 --> 43:53.422
[chuckles softly] Severe bleeding like this can lead to shock or even death,

565
43:53.506 --> 43:56.384
so it was lucky his friends got him to the hospital quickly.

566
43:56.467 --> 43:58.678
But all that bleeding out of nowhere...

567
43:59.595 --> 44:04.934
Could it be some kind of complication from his recent lung tumor surgery?

568
44:05.017 --> 44:06.686
Maybe something that's come back or...

569
44:06.769 --> 44:08.980
Hmm... It has nothing to do with his lungs.

570
44:09.063 --> 44:11.732
According to the endoscopy,

571
44:11.816 --> 44:15.778
the cause of the bleeding was a pretty big stomach ulcer.

572
44:15.862 --> 44:18.364
So he lost a lot of blood, and it was pretty serious.

573
44:18.447 --> 44:20.825
Why would he suddenly develop a stomach ulcer?

574
44:20.908 --> 44:24.245
Well, it's hard to pinpoint the exact cause,

575
44:24.328 --> 44:27.248
but peptic ulcers are common in people under a lot of stress,

576
44:27.331 --> 44:29.834
people who've been taking painkillers for a long time,

577
44:29.917 --> 44:32.170
and people who drink or smoke a lot.

578
44:33.337 --> 44:38.134
He needs to avoid stress, and absolutely no drinking or smoking.

579
44:39.302 --> 44:42.096
I see. Thank you.

580
44:52.356 --> 44:53.649
Mr. Kim Gyeongho.

581
44:53.733 --> 44:54.817
-Yes. -Come in.

582
45:00.448 --> 45:01.949
You're not children.

583
45:02.617 --> 45:06.037
How can you be so immature and irresponsible? Huh?

584
45:07.079 --> 45:10.791
You're all smart enough to get PhDs and even become professors someday.

585
45:11.792 --> 45:14.921
What's the point of being smart if you can't get your lives together?

586
45:15.713 --> 45:18.549
How are you supposed to teach students someday like this?

587
45:22.887 --> 45:23.930
And, Taeho,

588
45:24.722 --> 45:26.515
you really let me down.

589
45:27.975 --> 45:29.477
You're older than the other kids.

590
45:30.978 --> 45:32.355
I'm sorry.

591
45:32.438 --> 45:34.690
The other kids might not have known,

592
45:34.774 --> 45:37.985
but you've known Minjae the longest, and you're close with him.

593
45:38.069 --> 45:39.528
You know what he's been through.

594
45:40.863 --> 45:41.864
I'm sorry.

595
45:43.491 --> 45:46.285
Why did you have to let him drink so much when he's sick?

596
45:47.328 --> 45:49.497
[trembling] I really didn't know, I swear.

597
45:49.580 --> 45:54.543
I just found out today that he had surgery and went through chemo in Canada.

598
45:56.045 --> 46:00.883
Hey, why didn't you tell us if you knew about it?

599
46:01.717 --> 46:03.010
Well...

600
46:03.094 --> 46:06.430
Minjae told me not to tell anyone.

601
46:06.514 --> 46:09.934
Hey, you still should've told us.

602
46:10.017 --> 46:12.895
Why can't you figure out what to say and what not to say?

603
46:15.231 --> 46:18.651
You know what? Somehow, you never say the things you should

604
46:18.734 --> 46:20.945
and always say the things you shouldn't.

605
46:21.028 --> 46:24.907
Right. You said this weird thing about Minjae and his mother earlier, too.

606
46:26.367 --> 46:27.827
What weird thing?

607
46:28.536 --> 46:30.162
No, it's nothing.

608
46:30.246 --> 46:32.039
What do you mean, nothing?

609
46:32.123 --> 46:36.502
You saw Minjae and his mother together and said something weird about them.

610
46:36.585 --> 46:38.504
And the whole lab went crazy over it.

611
46:38.587 --> 46:39.839
No.

612
46:39.922 --> 46:41.674
[Hangyeol] Minjae denied it,

613
46:41.757 --> 46:45.136
but you didn't believe him and said she touched him.

614
46:45.845 --> 46:48.973
You just kept insisting then.

615
46:50.141 --> 46:51.726
Saw what?

616
46:51.809 --> 46:53.269
What are you guys talking about?

617
46:53.352 --> 46:54.353
No.

618
46:54.437 --> 46:57.565
We can't really tell you what,

619
46:57.648 --> 46:59.567
but he had the whole lab freak out.

620
47:01.944 --> 47:06.824
Does this mean Minjae was stressed out because of you?

621
47:06.907 --> 47:08.784
No, it wasn't because of me.

622
47:09.785 --> 47:13.789
Minjae got sick and threw up blood because of you, man.

623
47:23.090 --> 47:26.844
That's it. I don't want you seeing Minjae anymore.

624
47:27.887 --> 47:28.888
Pardon?

625
47:29.805 --> 47:32.725
I'll tell Professor Ahn about it.

626
47:32.808 --> 47:35.811
What? Tell Professor Ahn what...

627
47:39.190 --> 47:40.733
Wait, Minjae...

628
47:41.567 --> 47:43.694
didn't throw up blood because of me.

629
47:51.035 --> 47:52.787
It's all because of Lim Youjin.

630
47:52.870 --> 47:54.622
[Taeho scoffs] What about Youjin?

631
48:00.044 --> 48:03.005
Minjae and Lim Youjin were secretly dating.

632
48:05.132 --> 48:06.884
They kept it under wraps,

633
48:08.844 --> 48:11.430
but then they broke up when Minjae left for the States.

634
48:11.514 --> 48:15.351
Then when he came back to Korea, he still wasn't over her

635
48:15.434 --> 48:17.269
and asked her to get back together.

636
48:17.353 --> 48:19.146
But she said no.

637
48:19.230 --> 48:22.608
Because she's seeing someone else now.

638
48:26.445 --> 48:31.575
That's why Minjae got stressed out, drank, and threw up blood.

639
48:35.996 --> 48:37.581
It's all because of Lim Youjin,

640
48:39.375 --> 48:40.418
not me.

641
49:25.421 --> 49:28.924
Hello, I'm here to visit a patient named Park Minjae.

642
49:30.342 --> 49:33.387
I heard he was taken to the ER last night and had surgery.

643
49:34.722 --> 49:35.723
Are you his family?

644
49:36.599 --> 49:38.934
I'm not his family. I'm his junior from school.

645
49:39.018 --> 49:41.312
If you're not family, you can't visit him.

646
49:42.897 --> 49:45.232
His guardian asked for him not to have any visitors.

647
49:46.901 --> 49:47.902
I see.

648
49:52.865 --> 49:55.910
Then, can he eat something like porridge?

649
49:55.993 --> 49:57.077
Pardon?

650
49:57.161 --> 49:58.787
When I had my appendix out,

651
49:58.871 --> 50:01.624
I could start eating thin rice porridge after about 3 days.

652
50:02.416 --> 50:05.336
We can't give out that kind of information about a patient.

653
50:06.670 --> 50:08.297
I see. Thank you.

654
50:31.362 --> 50:33.822
[automated voice] The bus is arriving.

655
52:28.479 --> 52:32.024
Hello. I'm here to visit a patient named Park Minjae.

656
52:32.941 --> 52:35.361
Is he still not allowed to have visitors?

657
52:35.444 --> 52:39.490
If I can't see him, could you at least give him this porridge for me?

658
52:39.573 --> 52:40.824
One moment, please.

659
52:44.161 --> 52:48.165
Uh, I'm not seeing any record here.

660
54:45.324 --> 54:46.325
Hey.

661
54:46.408 --> 54:47.534
Hello.

662
54:47.618 --> 54:48.619
You're here.

663
54:51.497 --> 54:52.706
You're here, so come in.

664
54:52.789 --> 54:55.042
No, I don't need to.

665
54:55.125 --> 54:57.419
That's some porridge, though. You should have some.

666
54:58.462 --> 54:59.463
Oh!

667
55:01.131 --> 55:02.633
It's for me.

668
55:02.716 --> 55:04.218
Thanks, I appreciate it.

669
55:04.301 --> 55:05.302
Sure.

670
55:07.179 --> 55:09.556
-[elevator dings] -[automated voice] Going down.

671
55:09.640 --> 55:11.350
[Minjae] Bye. Have a safe trip home.

672
55:22.945 --> 55:25.072
Right...

673
55:25.155 --> 55:26.490
Do you want some juice?

674
55:27.032 --> 55:28.116
No, I'm fine.

675
55:29.117 --> 55:32.287
Okay, then let me make you a cup of hot tea.

676
55:32.371 --> 55:33.622
I'll just have water.

677
55:35.332 --> 55:36.625
Right. Okay.

678
55:39.002 --> 55:40.337
Let's see.

679
55:51.056 --> 55:52.057
Have a seat.

680
55:52.140 --> 55:53.141
Okay.

681
56:10.867 --> 56:12.077
-Hey. -Hey. Yeah?

682
56:12.828 --> 56:13.829
Go on.

683
56:13.912 --> 56:15.664
No, you go first.

684
56:16.290 --> 56:17.332
Ah.

685
56:19.376 --> 56:22.212
I was just going to say I appreciate the porridge.

686
56:23.589 --> 56:24.590
Oh...

687
56:27.593 --> 56:29.511
How are you doing after the surgery?

688
56:29.595 --> 56:30.804
Oh, that.

689
56:31.763 --> 56:34.141
I ended up with a hole in my stomach from drinking.

690
56:34.224 --> 56:35.934
Patching it up isn't even surgery.

691
56:38.228 --> 56:40.230
I'm supposed to be your senior.

692
56:40.314 --> 56:41.773
This is pretty embarrassing.

693
56:44.693 --> 56:46.486
But you shouldn't push yourself.

694
56:48.447 --> 56:50.741
Do you want me to help you with the unpacking?

695
56:51.867 --> 56:53.327
Oh, those?

696
56:53.410 --> 56:55.370
I'm not unpacking. I'm packing.

697
57:01.293 --> 57:02.419
I'm...

698
57:03.086 --> 57:04.755
I'm going back to Canada.

699
57:06.715 --> 57:07.716
What?

700
57:08.717 --> 57:09.718
Why?

701
57:12.429 --> 57:13.680
It's just...

702
57:14.640 --> 57:17.309
hard and painful for me to see you.

703
57:20.270 --> 57:21.772
And I don't like it here anymore.

704
57:26.026 --> 57:27.694
Then what about school?

705
57:28.945 --> 57:32.157
I'm quitting. I'm done with robotics, too.

706
57:34.534 --> 57:36.745
You're going to quit school and robotics?

707
57:36.828 --> 57:38.205
Then what are you going to do?

708
57:40.123 --> 57:42.250
That, I'll have to think about from now on.

709
57:46.004 --> 57:47.673
Are you threatening me right now?

710
57:48.632 --> 57:49.633
Threatening you?

711
57:51.093 --> 57:53.136
"I'm falling apart like this because of you,

712
57:53.220 --> 57:55.806
so you should take responsibility." That's what you mean.

713
58:01.019 --> 58:03.313
It is something like that, yeah.

714
58:09.653 --> 58:11.446
Do whatever you want.

715
58:11.530 --> 58:14.950
Whether you go to Canada or not, I don't care one bit.

716
58:15.992 --> 58:16.993
Yeah.

717
58:17.869 --> 58:21.289
You've always known exactly what you like and don't like.

718
58:22.207 --> 58:23.792
And you're stubborn, too.

719
58:23.875 --> 58:27.546
I know once you say something, you never take it back.

720
58:33.969 --> 58:37.431
They say time heals all wounds for a reason, you know.

721
58:39.933 --> 58:42.018
At first, you'll feel like you're going crazy.

722
58:42.102 --> 58:44.020
You won't be able to breathe or sleep.

723
58:46.648 --> 58:50.986
But then, you'll start breathing and sleeping again.

724
58:53.488 --> 58:57.200
You'll start craving food again, and all that.

725
59:00.579 --> 59:04.458
Then at some point, you'll look back and wonder, "Why was I so sad back then?"

726
59:06.001 --> 59:07.836
That day will come pretty soon.

727
59:18.221 --> 59:19.306
I'm sorry.

728
59:21.224 --> 59:22.809
I messed up.

729
59:24.603 --> 59:25.896
I don't want to hear it.

730
59:28.815 --> 59:29.941
I know.

731
59:30.984 --> 59:34.821
What I did was so wrong, it can't be forgiven or taken back.

732
59:37.157 --> 59:39.951
You see, at first,

733
59:40.035 --> 59:43.580
I tried to think of any way I could get you back.

734
59:45.874 --> 59:49.211
But then I realized there's no way you'll forgive me.

735
59:50.545 --> 59:53.465
Because I can't even forgive myself, any more than you can.

736
59:55.801 --> 59:59.805
Back then, I thought that was the best thing I could do.

737
01:00:01.223 --> 01:00:02.974
But looking back now,

738
01:00:04.768 --> 01:00:08.605
I did all that to protect my pride.

739
01:00:11.274 --> 01:00:12.400
I know.

740
01:00:13.985 --> 01:00:16.196
I know you did that because you were sick.

741
01:00:16.279 --> 01:00:17.364
No.

742
01:00:19.491 --> 01:00:23.453
I said I wanted to break up because of you, for your sake,

743
01:00:26.081 --> 01:00:27.749
but I think that was a lie too.

744
01:00:32.838 --> 01:00:35.090
Being with you...

745
01:00:36.967 --> 01:00:38.760
made me happy.

746
01:00:39.886 --> 01:00:43.098
It made me happy, but it also really scared me.

747
01:00:45.517 --> 01:00:47.727
I was scared that one day, it'd all end.

748
01:00:48.812 --> 01:00:50.272
And that I'd be abandoned.

749
01:00:51.106 --> 01:00:55.318
I was always holding back because I didn't want to get hurt,

750
01:00:56.903 --> 01:00:58.780
always finding excuses to run away.

751
01:01:02.784 --> 01:01:03.785
You said...

752
01:01:05.579 --> 01:01:08.540
losing me scared you more than dying, right?

753
01:01:10.458 --> 01:01:11.835
You said

754
01:01:13.670 --> 01:01:15.463
you thought you'd rather die.

755
01:01:25.432 --> 01:01:30.186
And I let you die because I didn't want to get hurt.

756
01:01:31.146 --> 01:01:32.147
So...

757
01:01:34.733 --> 01:01:39.070
I'm the most selfish coward in the world.

758
01:01:45.952 --> 01:01:47.621
Who did I think I was?

759
01:01:47.704 --> 01:01:49.623
You loved me so much,

760
01:01:51.625 --> 01:01:52.834
but I didn't.

761
01:01:55.253 --> 01:01:57.422
You loved me,

762
01:01:59.758 --> 01:02:01.009
but I didn't.

763
01:02:03.553 --> 01:02:04.554
No.

764
01:02:07.349 --> 01:02:08.642
You loved me.

765
01:02:10.644 --> 01:02:12.103
You loved me so much.

766
01:02:27.369 --> 01:02:29.746
Come on, I mean it.

767
01:02:32.248 --> 01:02:34.209
You have no idea how happy you made me.

768
01:02:36.002 --> 01:02:38.421
And how happy I am now.

769
01:02:41.716 --> 01:02:45.512
You have no idea how happy I am to have you back here

770
01:02:47.263 --> 01:02:49.015
by my side, safe and sound.

771
01:02:50.934 --> 01:02:52.727
And how much I love you.

772
01:03:01.611 --> 01:03:03.029
Get up. Look at me.

773
01:03:08.076 --> 01:03:09.452
Don't you trust me?

774
01:03:10.787 --> 01:03:12.664
Have you seen me lie?

775
01:03:13.707 --> 01:03:14.749
Yeah.

776
01:04:05.592 --> 01:04:09.512
BETWEEN STEPS

777
01:04:09.596 --> 01:04:12.599
[Youjin] If you thought I forgave it all, you're wrong.

778
01:04:12.682 --> 01:04:14.517
We're not back together.

779
01:04:15.226 --> 01:04:16.227
-Oh? -[groans]

780
01:04:16.311 --> 01:04:17.937
When did you get here?

781
01:04:18.021 --> 01:04:20.940
[Youjin] Thinking about me before going to bed. You can do that too.

782
01:04:21.024 --> 01:04:24.319
If they're Youjin's, why don't you give them to her yourself?

783
01:04:24.402 --> 01:04:25.987
[Jihoon] They're yours.

784
01:04:26.071 --> 01:04:29.199
[Minjae] Seriously, what are you going to do if I die?

785
01:04:29.282 --> 01:04:31.868
Youjin, I think this is it for us.

786
01:04:31.951 --> 01:04:34.537
Just like me. I said you could love me.

787
01:04:34.621 --> 01:04:36.831
[Minjae] Let's end this. I really want to stop doing this.
